meta {
  name: bookings export
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/administrator/bookings/export/?payment_status=paid&from=2026-09-01&to=2026-09-30
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  payment_status: paid
  from: 2026-09-01
  to: 2026-09-30
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  CSV download of the bookings list -- "Export CSV" in the DevPlan. Responds with
  `text/csv` and `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="vidaverde-bookings-20260905.csv"`.

  Accepts `payment_status`, `from` and `to`, same meanings as the bookings list.
  Streams with `.iterator()`, so a large export does not load everything into
  memory.

  `GET /administrator/leads/export/` is the equivalent for leads.

  ## API example response
  Purchased,Student,Email,Package,Amount,Payment status,Reference,Classes used,Classes total,Expires
  2026-09-05 08:44,Marco Reyes,marco.reyes@example.com,Spanish Assessment & First Lesson,12.00,paid,pi_dummy_3603f68905934869ba494e38,1,1,2026-12-04
  2026-09-05 08:44,Ana Lopez,ana.lopez@example.com,Spanish Assessment & First Lesson,12.00,paid,pi_dummy_seed0000000000000,1,1,2026-12-04
}
